From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:55:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] DirectStorage: a worker keeps its source and intermediate
 buffers between requests

A compressed request allocated and zero-filled a buffer for its source,
and another for what zlib leaves for BCPack, hundreds of times a second.
Each worker keeps both now (up to 8 MiB each; a larger one is let go
after its request).

After upstream pull request #2981 by RVZO6. Its other half, a
decompressor kept per worker, is not needed here: this line inflates with
zlib-rs through a state kept per thread already.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
